    homework:'<p><b>Optional approved AWS sandbox only; billable.</b> Confirm current Region/API quotas/prices and a budget. Use only owned Classic bus/rules, test targets, narrow role/resource/KMS permissions and Standard delivery DLQ. Verify positive/negative pattern cases, per-entry ingestion failures, permission denial and actual target logs/data. Create a timezone-aware Scheduler target and verify real invocation after the expected minute window. Deploy reviewed idempotent TEST workers and Standard/Express definitions; measure actual retry, callback/deadline, pending refund and restart outcomes without real customer/provider money. Do not claim emulator history proves runtime. Cleanup only owned schedules/groups, rules/targets/buses, state machines/executions where supported, functions/roles, queues/DLQs, logs/alarms and test tables; account for retention charges. New Custom Event Bus subscriber practice needs its own scoped setup/retention/cost review.</p>',
    cards:[{front:'Three separate proofs?',back:'Ingestion accepted, target/API accepted and durable business outcome. HTTP200 or workflow success alone is insufficient.'},{front:'Classic versus current Custom Event Bus?',back:'Default/Classic uses rules/targets; newer Custom Event Bus uses retained events/subscribers and different order/dedup/API/pricing. Specify exact contract.'},{front:'Typed pattern traps?',back:'Numeric strings are not numbers; null/false/zero are present; strict > excludes boundary. Keys AND, leaf alternatives OR.'},{front:'Target permission paths?',back:'Current Lambda/SNS/SQS targets can use execution role or resource policy. This mission chooses exact events.amazonaws.com/rule SourceArn resource policies.'},{front:'Scheduler trap?',back:'Timezone and60secondprecision; OFF flexible window is not exact second. Role trust SourceArn scopes schedule GROUP; target/DLQ permissions separate.'},{front:'Standard/Express semantics?',back:'Standard execution model except explicit Retry; async Express at-least-once, sync Express at-most-once. External idempotency remains separate.'},{front:'Saga success means fulfilled?',back:'No. Compensation can produce a refunded outcome; failed compensation remains unresolved. Preserve stable identity and durable recovery phases.'},{front:'What did lab18 prove?',back:'Actual Classic→SQS routing, control-plane metadata and host DynamoDB phase/restart behavior. Default Moto ASL history synthetic; external payments0.'}]
